From d6b1876d909c8a8028c46b1298212b96bbfdeb1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:41:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: choose the Dolby Vision output of the video that
 plays

The video settings of the player (OSD > Settings > Video settings) get
"Dolby Vision output (this video)" for a Dolby Vision video: native Dolby
Vision (or "As the settings say" where the display does not take it),
Dolby Vision as HDR10 (mapped to the display where that is set), or
without Dolby Vision, as Kodi plays it. It is for that video only: the next
file starts with what the settings say (DVBRIDGE::NewVideo()).

"Without Dolby Vision" is not offered where the base layer is no picture by
itself (profile 5, and profile 10 compatible with nothing,
BaseLayerIsNoPicture()): played as Kodi plays it, it has the wrong colours,
which is why such a stream is reconstructed where it is not sent natively.
VideoPlayer says which stream opened
(DVBRIDGE::VideoStreamOpened()), and OutputChoiceOffered() decides.

Whether a stream is sent natively, reconstructed or played as Kodi plays it
is decided where its video stream opens: VideoPlayer (the display mode),
the decoder factory and the decoder (what each picture keeps). So a choice
opens the video stream again at the time it is at, as choosing another
video stream does (CVideoPlayer::SetVideoStream()); the file, the audio
and the subtitles stay open. The decoder marks its pictures with the choice
it was opened with (VideoPicture::doviNoNative): the pictures decoded before
keep the output they had, and the renderer changes the output once, with
the first picture of the stream opened again, instead of once for the
choice and once more for the new decoder.

Fail closed: what cannot be had now (the display does not take HDR10, the
conversion already failed in this video, no video stream to open again) is
not tried; the video goes on as it was, a notification says so, and the
list shows the previous choice again. A choice that is taken and then fails
when the output is set up falls back as any video does, to the ordinary
output. The Dolby Vision page of the player information gives "another
output was chosen for this video" as the reason.

The strings are translated in Estuary (31761-31768) into Spanish, as the
other strings of Hades are (CGUIUtils::GetHadesString()).
